Hi,

I've re-created the subversion repository at sourceforge for the selinux
core userland components, so anyone with a working copy will need to
make a fresh checkout.  This was to populate the repository with history
from a cvs tree, which wasn't working properly when I first created the
subversion repo at sourceforge back in May.

You can check out a fresh copy via:
	svn co https://svn.sourceforge.net/svnroot/selinux/trunk selinux

If you check out a full copy of selinux/ rather than just trunk/, be
warned that there are quite a few tags now (these can be browsed at
http://svn.sourceforge.net/viewvc/selinux/tags), generated by cvs2svn.  

Unless there is some reason to preserve cvs access, we will stop
updating the cvs repo very soon and will only maintain the svn repo.  We
will also disable cvs for the project at that time, which doesn't make
the cvs data inaccessible but does drop it from view on the project page
to avoid confusing new users.  We'll also update the project page to
refer to the svn repo instead of the cvs one.

